<title>USA: Weirton Steel has tentative nurse agreement.</title>
<headline>Weirton Steel has tentative nurse agreement.</headline>
<dateline>WEIRTON, W.Va. 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Weirton Steel Corp said Tuesday it has reached a tentative contract agreement with its nursing staff which is represented by the Independent Steelworkers Union.</p>
<p>The accord marks the third and final contract to be negotiated between the company and the union, Weirton said.</p>
<p>A ratification vote by the three bargaining groups on their respective tentative agreements is expected in the near future. The length of each contract is 4-1/2 years.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, negotiations continue between the steelmaker and the Independent Guard Union.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
</text>
